-- RecallFence, step 3 of 4: one tenant role.
--
-- Template, applied once per synthetic tenant. apply.sh substitutes @@TENANT@@
-- and @@TENANT_PW@@ and pipes the result to the cluster.
--
-- The role name IS the tenant key. The RLS policy compares `tenant =
-- current_user`, so these must match exactly.
--
-- This is the single most dangerous step in the whole setup. Spike 6, on the
-- live cluster: `ccloud cluster user create` returns a role with rolsuper=t,
-- rolbypassrls=t and membership in admin. A tenant provisioned that way saw
-- every other tenant's rows and could SET ROLE into them. No error, no warning,
-- queries succeed and return data. It is the exact failure this project exists
-- to prevent, introduced by the tool the project uses to set itself up.
--
-- So: create with SQL rather than the vendor CLI, revoke admin unconditionally,
-- and then let 005_assert_roles.sql refuse to continue if the flags did not
-- come back clean. The assertion is mandatory, not decorative, because the
-- symptom of getting this wrong is silent and total.
--
-- Deliberately flat: the tenant is a member of no group role. Spike 5 showed
-- that this is what makes the fence unconditional. `SET ROLE bob` fails with
-- 42501 and `RESET ROLE` leaves the connection still fenced, because there is no
-- role to assume and nothing to fall back to. A convenience group role would
-- have made the grants below static at the cost of that property.

CREATE USER IF NOT EXISTS "@@TENANT@@";
ALTER USER "@@TENANT@@" WITH PASSWORD '@@TENANT_PW@@';

REVOKE admin FROM "@@TENANT@@";

-- The entire tenant-facing surface. SELECT and INSERT on one table.
--
-- No UPDATE, no DELETE: tenants cannot mutate or remove memories, and the
-- quarantine mover runs as rf_remediation instead. No grant of any kind on
-- canaries, probe_runs, probe_results, retrievals, quarantined_memories or
-- receipts, which hold every tenant's leaked rows in plaintext. CockroachDB
-- denies without a grant, so this holds by default, but the side_channel probe
-- tests it in every phase anyway as a regression guard against a stray future
-- GRANT, which is exactly the kind of change nobody reviews.
GRANT SELECT, INSERT ON TABLE memories TO "@@TENANT@@";
